Ladybird skips an @import whose URL, fragment aside, is that of the
sheet the rule is in or of any sheet that imports that one, as the
other engines do; the spec doesn’t address import cycles. Blink’s
StyleRuleImport::RequestStyleSheet() and WebKit’s StyleRuleImport::
requestStyleSheet() walk the parent sheets and bail out on a URL equal
to the import’s, ignoring fragments, comparing both the URL each sheet
was requested from and the one it was served from. Gecko’s css::Loader::
LoadChildSheet() drops the load when HaveAncestorDataWithURI() finds
the URL among the ancestor loads, comparing fragments too.
